.TH "REPROCTL\-STOP" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-stop \- stop services or tear down Tilt
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl stop\f[R] [\f[I]service\f[R]\&...]
| \f[B]\(enall\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stop running services or tear down the entire Tilt session.
.PP
Without \f[B]\(enall\f[R], the specified services are removed from the
active service configuration.
If no services remain after removal, Tilt is stopped automatically.
.PP
With \f[B]\(enall\f[R], the Tilt daemon is stopped entirely, tearing
down all running services regardless of which context started them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\(enall\f[R]
Stop the Tilt daemon entirely instead of removing individual services.
.TP
\f[B]\(enpick\f[R], \f[B]\-p\f[R]
Interactively select a service to stop.
Uses \f[B]fzf\f[R] if installed, otherwise a numbered prompt.
When no service names are given and stdin is a terminal, the picker is
shown automatically.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl stop api\-server
Remove api\-server from the running set.
.TP
reproctl stop \(enall
Tear down Tilt and all services.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[B]reproctl\f[R](1), \f[B]reproctl\-start\f[R](1),
\f[B]reproctl\-restart\f[R](1)
